sp.l:
          Good madam, stay awhile; I will be 
faithful. [Reads. 




                'Doubt thou the stars are fire; 


                Doubt that the sun doth move; 


                Doubt truth to be a liar; 


                But never doubt I love. 


                'O dear
          Ophelia, I am ill at these numbers; I have not art to reckon my groans: but that I love thee best, O most best, believe it. Adieu.  'Thine evermore, most
          dear lady, whilst  this machine is to him, HAMLET.

sp.p:
   Why, any thing, but to the purpose. You were sent for;
and there is a kind of confession in your looks which your
modesties have not craft enough to colour: I know the good king and queen have sent for you.
